# Everything, then back what the build actually needs. A deny list eventually lets a stale bin/ or a
# local secrets file into a layer; an allow list cannot.
*

!Directory.Build.props
!Directory.Packages.props
!src/
!content/
# MUI.Catalog embeds these, so leaving them out builds an assembly whose migration set is empty and
# a site that starts against a database with no schema. MUI.Catalog.csproj now refuses to compile
# without them; this is the other half of that.
!migrations/

# Restored packages and previous outputs from a build on the host. Copying them in would let a
# locally built assembly outrank the one this image compiles, which is the failure that produces an
# image nobody can reproduce.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/*.user
**/appsettings.*.local.json
